+## Failure during session initialization
+
+- If `beforeSession` throws an `Error`, the turn awaits `onError(session, error)` and then `afterSession(session)` before rejecting with that same error, provided those hooks complete normally; both hooks receive the original session, and user-input and model-response hooks do not run ([validated by: reports and cleans up a failed beforeSession before rejecting with the original error](../../src/orchestration/beforeSessionFailure.acceptance.test.ts#L8)).
+
+`afterSession` is cleanup for an attempted turn, not proof that initialization succeeded or a model responded. It runs even if `beforeSession` only partially allocated resources. A deployer must track its own successful allocations and release only those; no new lifecycle argument is introduced. This is the guarantee required by #94, replacing the previously recorded bypass of both failure hooks.
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
-These three properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
